From 3dbc867595033dcc0974bdc7ccc90b7133d58b0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mshresponse <9147626+mshresponse@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 02:38:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use describe-verified relationship names; fix description
 length and titleColor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First deploy against a real Net Zero Cloud org surfaced three separate
problems. The object and field renames all validated — Standalone_Carbon_
Footprints and Standalone_Vehicle_Energy_Uses passed with no errors, which
confirms StnryAssetCrbnFtprnt, FootprintStage, TotScope1EmissionsInTco2e,
TotScope2LocBasedEmissions, TotScope2MktBasedEmissions, VehicleAssetEnrgyUse,
FuelConsumption and Distance.

Relationship names, read from a describe rather than guessed:
  StnryAssetEnvrSrc    -> CarbonFootprints          (was StnryAssetCrbnFtprnts)
  StnryAssetCrbnFtprnt -> StationaryAssetEnergyUses (was StnryAssetEnrgyUses)

Salesforce derives these from object labels, not from the abbreviated API
names, so the conventional plural was never going to match. Child
relationship names are not published in the object reference and are not
returned by a metadata retrieve; describe is the only source.

Account has no relationship to Supplier in a Net Zero Cloud org — the object
exists but is not wired to Account — so Accounts_with_or_without_Suppliers is
replaced by Stationary_Assets_with_without_Energy_Use, which uses the
describe-verified StnryAssetEnvrSrc -> StationaryAssetEnergyUses join. It
answers a comparable question: assets carrying no consumption data at all,
which is an earlier gap than a missing footprint.

Also fixes two defects of my own making: report descriptions of 336 and 279
characters against a 255 limit, and a missing required titleColor on the
dashboard (absent from the original file too, so it would have failed
regardless). titleColor is placed after title because the Metadata API is
order-sensitive there.

